# =============================================================================
# ROC AI Vision — .gitignore
# =============================================================================
# Strategy: ship SOURCE only. Everything large / reproducible / generated /
# vendor-binary stays out. The README + docs/build_directml.md document how
# to re-fetch the redistributables on a fresh clone.
# =============================================================================

# -------------------- Build artefacts ---------------------------------------
# CMake produces a `build/` (or `build_*/`) tree per sub-project. All
# regenerable from source via `cmake -S . -B build`.
build/
build_*/
out/
**/CMakeFiles/
**/CMakeCache.txt
**/cmake_install.cmake
**/install_manifest.txt
**/compile_commands.json
**/*.ninja
**/.ninja_*

# Compiled binaries + libraries
*.o
*.obj
*.a
*.lib
*.dll
*.exe
*.pdb
*.exp
*.ilk
*.so
*.so.*
*.dylib

# -------------------- Third-party redistributables --------------------------
# DirectML NuGet (~193 MB) + ORT-DML NuGet (~15 MB) + extracted DLLs +
# repackaged ort_dml_root. All re-downloadable via the steps in
# `docs/build_directml.md`. Single file limit on GitHub is 100 MB; the
# DirectML NuGet zip alone breaks that.
third_party/

# -------------------- ML model weights --------------------------------------
# .onnx files are big (10–45 MB each) and often derivative works of
# upstream models with their own licenses. We ship the .yaml manifests
# (kilobytes) so the dashboard can render the *structure* of the model
# zoo, but the weights themselves must be sourced separately by the
# operator. See `scripts/scan_onnx_to_manifest.py` for bulk generation.
models/*.onnx
**/*.onnx

# (manifests intentionally kept — they're plaintext YAML)

# -------------------- Node / SvelteKit --------------------------------------
dashboard/node_modules/
dashboard/.svelte-kit/
dashboard/build/
dashboard/.output/
dashboard/dist/
dashboard/coverage/
**/node_modules/

# Vite / Svelte stat caches
**/.vite/
**/.vinxi/

# npm / pnpm / yarn lockfiles for sub-projects are kept; debug logs are not.
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

# -------------------- Python tooling ----------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Jupyter checkpoints
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# -------------------- IDE / editor / OS -------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Cursor-specific noise (settings / chat scratch). The .cursor/rules/ tree
# IS source-controlled because it encodes binding rules; nothing else is.
.cursor/cache/
.cursor/logs/

# -------------------- Test + log outputs ------------------------------------
test_logs/
*.log
*.tmp
*.bak
*.orig

# Coverage reports
*.gcda
*.gcno
*.gcov
coverage/
htmlcov/

# -------------------- Generated screenshots / assets ------------------------
# The assets/ folder contains user-pasted screenshots from chat sessions —
# not part of the source tree.
assets/

# -------------------- Local secrets -----------------------------------------
*.pem
*.key
*.pfx
*credentials*
*.secret

# -------------------- Misc orchestrator runtime spew ------------------------
core/*.dll
core/*.exe
core/*.pdb
